{"id":681,"root":"نسك","bw":"nsk","tr":"n-s-k","found":true,"html":"<div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\">  <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">نَسَكَ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span> <em>He worshipped:</em> used transitively. See an ex. in a verse of El-Aashà, in the S, art. <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">نصب</span>. See 5. </div><div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\">  <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">أَنْسَكَ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span> [app. <em>He washed and purified</em> a garment]. (TA voce <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">اِجْتَابَ</span>.) </div><div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\">  <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">تَنَسَّكَ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span> <em>He devoted himself to religious exercises; applied himself to devotion;</em> (S, Msb, K:) as also ↓ <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">نَسَكَ</span> (S, K) and ↓ <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">نَسُكَ</span>: (K:) or the last, <em>he became a</em> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">نَاسِك</span>. (S.) </div><div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\"> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">نَسِيكَةٌ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span>: see <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">عَقِيقَةٌ</span>. </div><div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\"> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">مَنَاسِكُ الحَجِّ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span> <em>The religious rites and ceremonies of the pilgrimage:</em> or <em>the places where those rites and ceremonies are performed.</em> (Msb.) </div>","pages":null,"shownPages":null,"chars":1255,"entries":5,"shownEntries":5,"truncated":false,"match":"direct","key":"nsk"}